      "result": {
        "reply_text": "I understand that you bought a phone charger for 800 rupees in October 2026, it is not working, and you have already contacted support without success.\n\nUnder the law, you may bring a product liability action against a manufacturer or seller if a product is defective. A manufacturer is liable if the product has a manufacturing defect or does not conform to an express warranty.\n\nYou can register your grievance at the pre-litigation stage through the National Consumer Helpline (NCH). You can call the toll-free number 1915, use the NCH app, or visit the website consumerhelpline.gov.in. You can also reach out via WhatsApp at 8800001915 or email at nch-ca@gov.in.\n\nIf the issue is not resolved, you may file a formal complaint with the District Commission. The District Commission has jurisdiction to handle complaints where the value of goods or services does not exceed fifty lakh rupees. You can file this complaint where you reside or where the opposite party carries on business.\n\nPlease keep your bill and any records of your communication with the company support team as proof for your complaint.\n\nCould you please provide the name of the company that manufactured or sold the charger and the order ID for your purchase?\n\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 83\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 84\nSource: National Consumer Helpline Grievance Redressal Procedure, procedure 1\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 34\nSource: Consumer Protection (Jurisdiction of the District Commission, the State Commission and the National Commission) Rules, 2021, rule 3\nSource: Consumer Protection Act, 2019, section 35\n\nWhat I could not verify:\n- where to complain (if NCH and District Commission are not suitable)\n\nThis is legal information, not legal advice.",
